UMABOND Product Range Explained – Rubber Solutions for Different Industries


Industrial rubber products cover a wide range of applications, from vibration control in heavy machinery to sealing solutions in doors and windows. UMABOND, a rubber manufacturing company based in India, has built its product catalog around this variety, offering multiple categories of rubber and silicone products that serve different industries including construction, automobile, railway, and material handling.

One of the main product lines UMABOND offers is anti vibration mounts. These are used to absorb shocks and reduce vibration transfer between machine parts, which is important for both equipment longevity and operator safety. UMABOND's anti vibration mounts cover a wide load capacity range, starting from as low as 10kg and going up to 10000kg, which means the product line can serve both small equipment applications and heavy industrial machinery. This kind of range is useful for buyers who need a single reliable supplier rather than sourcing different capacity mounts from different vendors.

Rubber springs are another product category in their lineup. Similar to anti vibration mounts, rubber springs are used in machinery where load handling and shock absorption matter, particularly in material handling equipment. Rubber springs offer a different kind of flexibility compared to traditional metal springs, and in certain applications, they can be a more suitable choice depending on the operating environment.

Silicone profiles and silicone tubing form another significant part of UMABOND's offerings. This includes silicone solid profiles and silicone sponge profiles, which are used in applications requiring heat resistance and flexibility, such as pharmaceutical and food grade uses. Silicone materials are generally chosen when standard rubber compounds cannot handle the temperature range or chemical exposure involved in a particular application, so having a dedicated silicone product line adds versatility to what UMABOND can offer its clients.

Moulded rubber products are also part of the catalog, covering customized rubber parts designed for specific client requirements. Since UMABOND has in-house moulding capability along with machining support including VMC and CNC equipment, they are able to handle custom moulded parts without depending on third party vendors for tooling or machining work.

Extruded rubber products round out another major category, which includes profiles made from Natural rubber, Nitrile, EPDM, and more recently silicone extrusions as well. Extruded rubber is commonly used for sealing applications, gaskets, and door seals, among other uses. UMABOND specifically highlights their door seal products as offering durability and reliability for construction applications, where consistent sealing performance matters over time.

Self adhesive foam strips are another product offering, generally used in sealing and insulation applications where an easy-to-apply adhesive backed foam strip is more practical than a fully moulded or extruded part. These are commonly used in construction and other applications requiring quick installation without additional fixing hardware.

Rubber sheets complete the core product range, serving as a base material for a variety of industrial uses including flooring, lining, and general industrial applications where flat rubber material is needed in different thicknesses and compounds.

Across all these product categories, UMABOND positions itself around a few consistent points: full in-house manufacturing from raw material to finished product, ASTM-based testing standards, and a reported one-day lead time for around 90 percent of their orders. For businesses in industries like construction, automobile, railway, and material handling that require rubber components, having a single manufacturer that covers this breadth of product categories can simplify sourcing and reduce the number of vendors a business needs to manage.

